# BUGZ — Neural Swarm Simulation

BUGZ is a small Pygame and Box2D experiment in which simple circular creatures
move through a two-dimensional arena using a neural network. Each creature has
red-sensitive sensors, a set of thrust outputs, and a mutable morphology. A
standalone neural-network editor lets you inspect and change the network used by
the simulation.

This document describes the program as it currently works: how to run it, what
the controls do, how the simulation and network fit together, how to edit and
save a network, and where the main responsibilities live in the source.

